# Prebuilt toolchain assets ledger (release tag: toolchain-v1).
#
# Format: exactly one sha256sum line per triple (one self-contained tarball
# per triple; no separate sysroot asset):
#   <sha256>  corocc-toolchain-<triple>-gcc<gccver>-binutils<binutilsver>-glibc<glibcver>-ubuntu24.04.tar.gz
# The asset names are flat (no directories). Every archive carries a single
# tree at top level, corocc-toolchain/<triple>/{bin,lib,libexec,...,sysroot/},
# with the compiler at corocc-toolchain/<triple>/bin/<triple>-gcc and the
# sysroot at corocc-toolchain/<triple>/sysroot (relocatable -print-sysroot;
# the fetch probe path-normalizes both sides before comparing).
# scripts/ci/fetch-toolchain-assets.sh refuses to run when this file is
# missing, empty or has no entry for the requested triple, and rejects any
# matched line whose digest is not a 64-hex sha256 -- an empty or unfilled
# ledger must never fail open.
#
# The legacy two-tree family (separate corocc-sysroot-* and corocc-toolchain-*
# tarballs) is retired by the asset-layout ruling and has no lines here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset inventory (3 archives; sha256sum natural order). Built from source with
# gcc 13.3.0 / binutils 2.42 / glibc 2.39; each archive carries its license
# texts and SOURCES.txt provenance under share/licenses/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
7f5b96320477ed9dea494ac35fb51b95db3d39e7ed14245cc3e36157526b7b90  corocc-toolchain-aarch64_be-linux-gnu-gcc13.3.0-binutils2.42-glibc2.39-ubuntu24.04.tar.gz
16f6a9850fb34245dc8ff343758d116f03fbf28aed9a6ae5d6f33b42246caa5f  corocc-toolchain-armeb-linux-gnueabi-gcc13.3.0-binutils2.42-glibc2.39-ubuntu24.04.tar.gz
